@LibraryManagementSystem_HostAddress = http://localhost:5107

### 1. Search and filter books catalog (Story 3)
GET {{LibraryManagementSystem_HostAddress}}/api/books?query=clean&category=Software&page=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. List all book copies and statuses
GET {{LibraryManagementSystem_HostAddress}}/api/books/copies
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Add a new book (Story 1)
POST {{LibraryManagementSystem_HostAddress}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Refactoring",
  "isbn": "978-0134757599",
  "authorName": "Martin Fowler",
  "category": "Software Engineering",
  "publishedYear": 2018
}

###

### 4. Bind multiple physical copies to a book (Story 1)
POST {{LibraryManagementSystem_HostAddress}}/api/books/1/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "inventoryNumber": "INV-003"
}

###

### 5. CRUD Authors (Story 1)
GET {{LibraryManagementSystem_HostAddress}}/api/authors
Accept: application/json

###

### 6. Issue a loan (Story 4)
POST {{LibraryManagementSystem_HostAddress}}/api/loans/issue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookCopyId": 1,
  "readerId": 1
}

###

### 7. Reserve a currently borrowed book copy (Story 2)
POST {{LibraryManagementSystem_HostAddress}}/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookCopyId": 2,
  "readerId": 2
}

###

### 8. Check overdue readers (Story 2)
GET {{LibraryManagementSystem_HostAddress}}/api/loans/overdue-readers
Accept: application/json

###

### 9. Return a loan (triggers 48h hold + notification if reserved) (Story 2 & 4)
POST {{LibraryManagementSystem_HostAddress}}/api/loans/return
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "loanId": 1
}

###

### 10. View sent notifications (Story 2)
GET {{LibraryManagementSystem_HostAddress}}/api/reservations/notifications
Accept: application/json

###